GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_ReleaseProcess> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_ReleaseProcess> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#ReleaseProcess> ;
    narr:childCount "6"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "42b2874b7637a892bcc9157978f0c55755194270" ;
    narr:narration """The hub frames a release train governed by a mandatory signing gate. QuintonFairweather states that [every Meridian deployment now requires a signed release manifest](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1) before shipping, and grounds the rule in a concrete incident: [two unsigned artifacts reached staging last quarter](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2), which he names as the sole justification for the gate. XenaExpertgh records the gate's formal parameters — the [gate definition](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4), its [scope across staging and production](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5), and the [named owner](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_6) — all stamped as decisions under legitimate authority. The [broader narrative](narr:Narrative_SignedManifestGate) frames the signed manifest as a non-negotiable precondition entering as a settled operational rule rather than a proposal. The register splits between QuintonFairweather's plain-spoken causal account and XenaExpertgh's terse technical specification, but both converge on conservation value and authority-ranking footing. No dissent is present among the children; the only tension lives in the gap between the incident-driven justification and the rule's blanket scope.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_6> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_SignedManifestGate> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Every Meridian deployment now requires a signed release" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "We saw two unsigned artifacts reach staging" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "**Gate**: signed release manifest required for Meridian deploys" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "**Scope**: applies to staging and production" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "a signed manifest becomes a non-negotiable precondition for deployment" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_SignedManifestGate> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The incident narrative (two unsigned artifacts) is retrospective justification, while the gate is framed as a forward-looking blanket rule — the causal story and the rule's scope don't perfectly align." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_2> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The broader narrative asserts the gate is a settled operational rule, but no child tests whether it remains contestable or propositional." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_SignedManifestGate> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.2" .
